  "review_notes": "I read the whole file and grepped Mathlib for related declarations. HasConicalProducts is the enriched analogue of HasProducts. It is defined through HasConicalLimitsOfShape (Discrete J), so it builds on the existing conical-limit API. HasConicalProduct is an abbrev for HasConicalLimit V (Discrete.functor f), which parallels the non-enriched HasProduct. The closing example derives HasProducts from HasConicalProducts, so the two notions are connected. I found no independent competing definition, and I did not look further into the parallel non-enriched definitions.",
